Text=The Inquisition came out of the siege with the most intact command structure left in Barcelona, and the city handed it the rebuilding. You had risen high in the Holy Office, high enough that the work reached you as paper rather than as duty, and high enough to sign what other men then carried out. Its fires burned on through the peace exactly as they had burned through the war, because a frightened city asks its inquisitors for more work rather than less. The cities paid for the wood. Your signature was on enough of it that the archive eventually gave you a box of your own.
