Node ID=900 order none
Text=Every order came out of the siege smaller than it had gone in, and every one of them claimed the ending as its own. You had taken no oath and worn no mark, and there was no faction anywhere that could produce a document with your name on it. The Templars wrote that a knight had finished it. The Inquisition wrote that a faithful servant had. The Wielders wrote that one of their own had, and the Horde told it as a story about a westerner who had owed them a favour. All four accounts survive in the archives, and not one of them is true.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order england
Text=England spent that year waiting on Barcelona, and in the end the Armada never had to sail into a city that was already burning. You had carried the Crown's business through the Port District while the fleet was still in harbour, inside a conspiracy that would have hanged you in any week of it. Guy Fawkes' promise was kept the way such promises are kept: a pension paid out of an account with another man's name on it, a quiet word in two ports, and no record anywhere of the reason for either. He was hanged for something else, years later, and said nothing about you.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 order omalley
Text=Grace O'Malley kept her ships, her harbour and her true name, and the Crown learned none of the three from you. You had been given more than her silence to hold, at a point where selling it would have cost you nothing and paid well. She was still taking prizes off the Irish coast twenty years after Barcelona, under the name she had chosen rather than the one she was born to. Her crews told the Barcelona story the entire time, with you in it, and told it badly, and she never once corrected them.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
