------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend cervantes
Text=Miguel de Cervantes went home with his quill and without the beast, and could not have explained either to anybody who asked. He had kept notes on every road you walked, and the notes outlasted the hunt by four hundred years. Years later he published a long book about a madman who believed himself a knight, sold it badly, and was copied everywhere. He never once set a scene in Barcelona and never wrote down what the quill was. He died in Madrid, in debt, and is buried somewhere nobody has since managed to find.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend cervantes dead
Text=Cervantes was buried where he fell with the quill still on him, and whoever went through his pockets could not read. A bookseller in Valladolid later claimed to have owned a manuscript about a madman who believed himself a knight, could never produce it, and was not believed. The book was never written. A Templar inventory of his effects lists four notebooks, a sword he could not have lifted, and one quill, and values the quill at nothing at all. The beast was still out there, and nobody else had ever seen it either. His brother collected nothing, there being nothing to collect.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend cervantes dead alone
Text=Cervantes died in Barcelona with the quill still on him, and no book was written and no beast was hunted. The quill went into an evidence chest in the Chambers of the Inquisition, entered by a clerk as a quill, and is presumably there yet. Nobody in Spain has heard of him. Don Quixote de la Mancha exists in no library anywhere, and the gap it leaves is not shaped like anything, so nobody has ever noticed that it is missing, and nobody ever will. The beast was never found either, by him or by anybody who came after him.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
