------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend cervantes alone
Text=You listened to him about the beast and left him to it, which is what the whole Port District had been doing for a year. He hunted it alone, was arrested for what he did to a wall while hunting it, and was released once the Templars decided he was harmless rather than heretical. He published anyway. The book is about a madman who believed himself a knight, and the man who wrote it had been followed down the street by one, and no reader has ever needed to know that to laugh at it.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 shade feather
Text=You told Don Quixote what he was and he believed you, which is the only argument anybody won in Barcelona that year. He asked whether there had been quests he would not now get to, was told that there had been, and took it a great deal better than the man who made him would have. A single feather came down where he had been standing, went along the floor, and out under the door. Cervantes did not write about it and did not pick the quill up again for eleven years. The book, when it finally came, is about a man whom nobody had conjured.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 shade killed
Text=You killed Don Quixote in front of the man who had made him, and Cervantes watched it without saying anything and then talked about it for thirty years. There was no body, and they buried something anyway, in a plot the parish never charged for because the parish never established what was in it. He had asked only that you address him correctly, and you had, every time, which he mentioned to Cervantes more than once. He said he was a slayer of dragons. By the end that was nearly true. Nobody in the Port District ever asked what was in the coffin.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 shade persists
Text=Don Quixote was still at it twenty years later, by which time he had outlasted most of the people who had found him funny. He kept to the Port District, challenged whatever he was given to challenge, and was fed by a tavern that had decided he was good for custom and billed the city for his stool twice. Nobody ever told him what he was, and Cervantes never did either, which may have been cowardice and may have been the kindest thing either of them managed. He is in the book. He does not know.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
