Node ID=900 friend joan dead
Text=Jehanne d'Arc died away from the Crypt she had held for nine years, which she would have counted as the worse of the two losses. The Bleeding Lance went to whoever reached the chamber next and the Templars did not record who. Her certainty was the thing people remembered and the thing they got wrong: it had never been about France, she had said so plainly, and France was written into it anyway. A chapel outside Orleans carried her name within a century, built by men who could not have named the relic she died for.
Should Have Voiceover=1

