Node ID=900 friend roger
Text=Sir Roger Templeton went back to an England that had changed sides while he was out of it, and spent his remaining service explaining to Templars younger than himself that the druids had once fought beside them. He was believed by about half. He kept the habit of addressing people by rank, including you, including long after it had stopped being accurate. The Shrine was sealed, properly this time, by men he had personally argued into doing it. He is in the order's rolls as having died in Spain, which he found funny and never corrected.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
