Node ID=900 friend grumdjum
Text=Grumdjum got his verse. He had been threatening you with poetry for a year and he delivered, at length, in a hall full of goblins who had never been further east than the pass. The poem is accurate about the fighting and ruinous about everything else, and you are in it under a name he invented and would not explain. He outlived three Khans by the simple method of being the only goblin anyone wanted to hear from. Goblin children still recite the Alamut stanza, badly, and the stanza is wrong about Alamut. He dictated the last third of it, being by then far too grand to write.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
