------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend grumdjum dead
Text=Grumdjum died before he could finish it, which he would have called the single worst outcome available. The verses he had already made were remembered correctly for about ten years and then merged with four other poems about four other goblins. The composite hero is braver than Grumdjum and much less funny. Nobody who recites it knows that the best line in it, about a brave crusader who threatened to vanquish a knave, was written about you by a goblin who had decided he liked you and never once said so out loud. The hall he would have recited it in was still standing eighty years later and was never used for poetry again.
Should Have Voiceover=1

