Node ID=900 friend diego
Text=Bishop Diego's eyes went entirely inside two years and he kept working. He was given a reader and a boy to lead him and he outlasted both posts, hearing confession in a stone room in the Wilderness and getting more out of voices than he had ever got out of faces. He blessed you by name at the end of every conversation, including the ones in which you had told him nothing. The Inquisition left him there because he was useful and because moving him would have required somebody to make a decision. He called you *my child* to the last, being about ninety.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
