Node ID=900 friend diego defended
Text=You dealt with the Dark Inquisitors on his behalf and went on your way, and Bishop Diego kept his post and his failing eyes for another decade. He never learned how close the cult had come to buying his death, because the only man who could have told him was the man who had turned the offer down. He blessed you by name whenever you came back, having long since no idea what you looked like. The Inquisition left him there because he was useful and because moving him would have needed somebody to decide something.
