------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend darsh dead
Text=Inquisitor Darsh died out of the camp, and that was the most that could be said for it. The Inquisition recorded him lost in the Wilderness, which was accurate, complete, and about a tenth of the story. Nobody senior enough to be curious ever asked how he had got out of the goblin camp in the first place, so the part you did goes unrecorded in an archive that records everything. The last thing he said to you he had been saying to everyone for forty years, in exactly that tone: *you disappoint me, young one.*
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
