------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend darsh eaten
Text=Darsh was never taken out of the goblin camp, and the goblins did what goblins do. The Warrens argued for a fortnight afterwards about whether he had been better with the red spice or the grey, settled on the grey by a narrow margin, and still cite the argument as the time there was something in the Warrens worth arguing about. The Inquisition recorded him lost in the Wilderness. Raphael asked after him twice in eleven years and was told nothing, there being nothing anybody wished to put in writing. The Khan's daughter was not consulted and remembers the whole business differently.
Should Have Voiceover=1

