Node ID=900 friend fang
Text=The cub grew. He had come to you small enough to carry and ended the campaign big enough that strangers crossed the road, and he never learned to be quiet about either. He outlived most of the party, bears being durable and the Crossroads being a great deal safer than Alamut. Hunters in that country stopped working the eastern woods for a decade and gave reasons that got taller every year. He is in Grumdjum's poem, which calls him a demon, and in a Templar's report, which calls him *the beast, trained, in the company of the Scion*.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
