Node ID=900 friend golem
Text=The golem stopped. It had been made in England to break a line and spent its last campaign walking behind you instead, obeying instructions it gave no sign of understanding. When it finally stopped it was in a cave in the giants' country, upright, facing the way you had gone. The English makers' marks on the shoulder plate were still legible two centuries later, when a shepherd found it and took the arm for scrap. Nobody who saw it move ever agreed on whether it had been alive. It never once indicated a preference. The shepherd's family used the shoulder plate as a doorstep for sixty years.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CTriggerRelayAction
{
Relay Name=Fixt order epilogue relay
}
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=900 friend golem dead
Text=The golem was broken rather than stopped, which may or may not be a distinction. It came apart inside one piece of work, the way the English had built it to, and what was left would not have been worth a shepherd's trouble. Its makers were dead, its line was broken, and there was no second one anywhere. Whatever it had been doing when it chose to follow you, it was the last of its kind to do it, and there was nobody to ask and nothing left in it that could have answered. The English never built a second, the war having moved on to men.
Should Have Voiceover=1

Requirement=!None
